--- Number Error Branch Tester ---
--- Float overflow ---
PASS: float + float -> Arithmetic result is infinite (float overflow)
PASS: float - float -> Arithmetic result is infinite (float overflow)
PASS: float * int -> Arithmetic result is infinite (float overflow)
PASS: float / tiny -> Arithmetic result is infinite (float overflow)
PASS: float // tiny -> Arithmetic result is not finite
PASS: float % tiny stays finite
--- Division and modulo by zero ---
PASS: int % 0 -> Division by zero
PASS: float % 0 -> Division by zero
PASS: int // 0 -> Division by zero
PASS: float // 0.0 -> Division by zero
--- Floor division and modulo signs ---
PASS: -7 // 2
PASS: -7 % 2
PASS: 7.5 // 2
PASS: 7.5 % 2
PASS: 2 ** -2
--- Integer size limit (v is 2 ** 99999) ---
PASS: v + 1 is still allowed
PASS: v + v -> Arithmetic result too large (exceeds integer size limit)
PASS: v - (0 - v) -> Arithmetic result too large (exceeds integer size limit)
PASS: v * 2 -> Arithmetic result too large (exceeds integer size limit)
PASS: v * v -> Arithmetic result too large (exceeds integer size limit)
PASS: v / v
--- Huge integers mixed with floats ---
PASS: v / 1.5 -> Division result exceeds float range; use integer floor division (//) instead
PASS: v // 1.5 -> Invalid floor division operation
PASS: v % 1.5 -> Invalid modulo operation
PASS: v ** 0.5 -> int too large to convert to float
--- Mixed operand types ---
PASS: number + string concatenates
PASS: number * string repeats
PASS: number * list repeats
PASS: number - string -> Illegal operation
PASS: number // string -> Illegal operation
PASS: number % list -> Illegal operation
PASS: number / dict -> Illegal operation
PASS: number ** string -> Illegal operation
PASS: string & number -> Illegal operation
--- Powers and shifts ---
PASS: negative base, fractional exponent -> Math domain error: result is complex
PASS: negative shift -> Negative shift count
PASS: float operand to & -> Left operand must be an integer
PASS: shifting by 32 or more clears the value
